bug_descriptions |bug_id, line_num, content|
    web_render_nowrap_lead_space_after_space_not_collapsed_2026-11-27, 0, "Chrome 159: 'x <span style=white-space:nowrap> y</span><span class=b>' puts the box at 20 (the nowrap run's lead space collapses into 'x '); Simple 25. The lead-space charge (layout_engine.spl ~4749) skips nowrap runs, which measure the space into their box, so it is never collapsed. Fable review also measured 154 vs 149.81 on another fixture."

